{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1154461-gateway-lair-traits","id":1154461,"title":"Gateway Lair Traits","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-31T12:10:17-07:00","id":1154461,"title":"Gateway Lair Traits","content":"For my own reference and hopefully others', I've decided to compile a list of 'gateway' Lair Traits, the ones that are fairly easy to re-create by mundane means or Beast powers in order to impose the others on a location or open a pathway, regardless of the location's original features. Don't waste time and effort searching for locations resonant with your Lair, create them. Especially useful for nomadic Beasts and Broods or when a character or group is away from any known location that was used to create or strongly resembles any of their Chambers.<br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Blazing Light: fireworks or portable spotlight<br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Blizzard: Storm-Lashed</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Burning: fires, Dragonbreath</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Crosswinds: Storm-Lashed</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Crushing: Caught in the Webs, Crushing Coils, or Vengeful Earth (Satiety expenditure)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Darkness: cut off power, break lights, Death of Light</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Diseased: Plague Bearer</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Engulfing: Caught in the Webs, Crushing Coils, or Vengeful Earth (Satiety expenditure)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Extreme Cold: Storm-Lashed</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Extreme Heat: fires, Dragonbreath</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Downpour: sprinklers, Storm-Lashed</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Earthquake: Vengeful Earth (low Satiety)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Electrified: ripped power cables, Storm-Lashed</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Exposed: Weakness Exposed</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Fog: fires or smoke bombs</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Hurricane: Storm-Lashed</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Infected: Plague Bearer</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Isolated: You Are Alone</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Jagged: rubble from Cyclopean Strength or Titanic Blow</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Murmurs: sound effects, Siren's Treacherous Song</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">No Exits: Illusion of Safety (low Satiety)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Poor Light: cut off power, break lights, Death of Light</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Razored: broken glass or pieces of barbwire</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Slick: oil or other lubricants</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Stench: stink bombs or tear gas</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Stinging: pepper spray or tear gas, Infestation or Bugs Everywhere</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Swarm: vial of fruit flies, Infestation or Bugs Everywhere</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Thunderous: loud music or fireworks, Siren\u2019s Treacherous Song or Storm-Lashed</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Toxic: Basilisk's Touch</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Unstable: bag of marbles, Titanic Blow (Satiety expenditure) or Vengeful Earth</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> Any other ideas or suggestions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 05-03-2018, 05:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T13:08:25-07:00","id":1154486,"title":"","content":"The 'Blazing Light' trait is easy enough to make if you use a bright enough flashlight or lamp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10141-solaris","name":"Solaris","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10141_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T13:47:17-07:00","id":1154499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solaris</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1154461-gateway-lair-traits?p=1154486#post1154486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The 'Blazing Light' trait is easy enough to make if you use a bright enough flashlight or lamp.</div> </div> </div> </div>Excellent idea, how could I have missed this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T05:16:43-07:00","id":1154668,"title":"","content":"Siren's Treacherous Song can be used to trigger a chain off Thunderous","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T06:00:21-07:00","id":1154681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solaris</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1154461-gateway-lair-traits?p=1154486#post1154486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The 'Blazing Light' trait is easy enough to make if you use a bright enough flashlight or lamp.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd say you need full-on floodlights for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T06:00:21-07:00","id":1154682,"title":"","content":"sorry, double post","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T06:31:39-07:00","id":1154688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1154461-gateway-lair-traits?p=1154681#post1154681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'd say you need full-on floodlights for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>You may have a point, and of course stadium floodlights would often be far too bulky and fixed for a traveling Beast or Brood. The point of the exercise is to pick the Lair Traits a character would be able to activate anywhere with equipment carried in a backpack at most. I wonder if portable floodlights exist with LED technology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 11-01-2017, 12:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T06:32:33-07:00","id":1154689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1154461-gateway-lair-traits?p=1154668#post1154668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Siren's Treacherous Song can be used to trigger a chain off Thunderous</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, this is a good one. It spares even the need to carry a boombox or such around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T09:43:51-07:00","id":1154748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1154461-gateway-lair-traits?p=1154668#post1154668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Siren's Treacherous Song can be used to trigger a chain off Thunderous</div> </div> </div> </div>Storm-Lashed as well, I'd say. The wind could set it off if it's strong enough. But also any lightning strikes all be accompanied with thunder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T10:30:49-07:00","id":1154762,"title":"","content":"Well the right fireworks would probably be able to set off a number of lair conditions though you'd need to time it for stuff like blinding light and thunderous since those will only have a few seconds at while they'd be active whereas an ensuing fire will probably last a bit longer. You'd only need to carry one or two depending on the strength of the fireworks involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T07:07:50-07:00","id":1155042,"title":"","content":"I've updated the OP list according to input.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1154461-gateway-lair-traits?p=1154748#post1154748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Storm-Lashed as well, I'd say. The wind could set it off if it's strong enough. But also any lightning strikes all be accompanied with thunder.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another good idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1154461-gateway-lair-traits?p=1154762#post1154762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well the right fireworks would probably be able to set off a number of lair conditions though you'd need to time it for stuff like blinding light and thunderous since those will only have a few seconds at while they'd be active whereas an ensuing fire will probably last a bit longer. You'd only need to carry one or two depending on the strength of the fireworks involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, fireworks seem a a feasible way of triggering Blinding Light or Thunderous although as you say one would need to time them. Extreme Heat or Burning can be set by starting fires through various possible means. I'm uncertain if there is any portable lighting equipment that may qualify for Blazing Light so I'd say this would be a ST's call.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 11-02-2017, 10:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T08:21:17-07:00","id":1155067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1154461-gateway-lair-traits?p=1154688#post1154688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You may have a point, and of course stadium floodlights would often be far too bulky and fixed for a traveling Beast or Brood. The point of the exercise is to pick the Lair Traits a character would be able to activate anywhere with equipment carried in a backpack at most. I wonder if portable floodlights exist with LED technology.</div> </div> </div> </div>They do! One of my beasts uses a spotlight. Limited uses before the battery dies, and it's pretty obvious, but still a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T11:45:46-07:00","id":1155150,"title":"","content":"I'm told fire extinguishers are pretty cold if you get hit with the spray directly, so would going into the spray qualify for the freezing cold trait?<br /> <br /> Swarns: I actually did have to carry a few vials of bugs around one time in high school. (Genetics class we had to take notes on how many died each hour from alchohol poisoning.) Later project revealed two or three of those vials could store up a lovely little cloud of fruit flies.<br /> <br /> Razored: Take apart the barbs on a barbwire fence and you have some lovely improvised caltrops.<br /> <br /> Would a large bag of marbles qualify for the unstable condition? I mean depending on the enviorment of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T13:40:23-07:00","id":1155179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1154461-gateway-lair-traits?p=1155150#post1155150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm told fire extinguishers are pretty cold if you get hit with the spray directly, so would going into the spray qualify for the freezing cold trait?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm uncertain about this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Swarns: I actually did have to carry a few vials of bugs around one time in high school. (Genetics class we had to take notes on how many died each hour from alchohol poisoning.) Later project revealed two or three of those vials could store up a lovely little cloud of fruit flies. </div> </div> </div>It seems a lovely idea on paper but I wonder how much effort it is going to require for a Beast or Brood to make themselves supplied with a few vials of fruit flies at all times. Edit: it seems pet shops sell them, so little effort at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Razored: Take apart the barbs on a barbwire fence and you have some lovely improvised caltrops. </div> </div> </div>Outside of certain rural environments barbwire fences aren't that common. In urban environments it would often be simpler just to smash some glass and throw its broken pieces around. But I guess characters might keep themselves supplied with some barbwire they have cut or torn apart with their Strength-boosting Atavisms and throw it around to make improvised caltrops.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Would a large bag of marbles qualify for the unstable condition? I mean depending on the enviorment of course. </div> </div> </div>I think it would, although as you point out, it would only work in certain environments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 11-02-2017, 05:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T21:52:48-07:00","id":1155287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1154461-gateway-lair-traits?p=1155179#post1155179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Outside of certain rural environments barbwire fences aren't that common. In urban environments it would often be simpler just to smash some glass and throw its broken pieces around. But I guess characters might keep themselves supplied with some barbwire they have cut or torn apart with their Strength-boosting Atavisms and throw it around to make improvised caltrops.</div> </div> </div> </div>$80 bucks US will buy 1320 feet of barbed wire. So I mean probably not have it shipped to your place, but not impossible to get in less rural areas.<br /> <br /> Not that raiding a recycle bin and some trash cans for a few discarded bottles wouldn't work and be fairly cheap too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3400,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","user":"nalak42","date":". 11-03-2017, 12:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T06:25:21-07:00","id":1155366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1154461-gateway-lair-traits?p=1155287#post1155287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">$80 bucks US will buy 1320 feet of barbed wire. So I mean probably not have it shipped to your place, but not impossible to get in less rural areas.<br /> <br /> Not that raiding a recycle bin and some trash cans for a few discarded bottles wouldn't work and be fairly cheap too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, absolutely. In order to prepare stuff to activate this Trait, beasts could buy some barbed wire, cut it or tear it apart with Cyclopean Strength or Titanic Blow, and carry the bits with the barbs. Alternatively, they can carry a few discarded bottles and smash them when they need some broken glass.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T06:44:36-07:00","id":1155370,"title":"","content":"Not to rain on any parades, but.. I dunno, would those work?<br /> <br /> It has to mechanically match the environmental tilt, AND be an AoE or it wouldn't even qualify as an environmental tilt. I don't thing jars of bugs, especially fruitflies, would qualify. Some lair traits look easy from the name, but turn out a bit harder to get a full on Environmental Tilt out of. I kinda wish a few had been combined for mechanical grace and balance. Poor lighting and a few others do very similar things, I wish it had been merged into Poor Visibility, for example. Iirc, Mirages sounded great, but it was actually weaker than a lot of weaker lair traits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T08:25:20-07:00","id":1155403,"title":"","content":"Preparing a few areas for lair similarity is ideal, but being able to create similarity of at least some sort on the fly is a good deal. I think that a sufficient amount of broken things scattered over an area could easily simulate razored, but I'd rule that you need to spend your action spreading them before it was enough.<br /> <br /> I'm now imagining a beast who uses a Sunforce spotlight with a disco ball.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T11:31:17-07:00","id":1155462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1154461-gateway-lair-traits?p=1155370#post1155370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to rain on any parades, but.. I dunno, would those work?<br /> <br /> It has to mechanically match the environmental tilt, AND be an AoE or it wouldn't even qualify as an environmental tilt. I don't thing jars of bugs, especially fruitflies, would qualify. Some lair traits look easy from the name, but turn out a bit harder to get a full on Environmental Tilt out of.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, RAW indicates sprinklers would suffice to activate Downpour, so by analogy some serious leeway in intensity is usually allowed between the Lair Trait and its equivalent environmental condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T11:33:10-07:00","id":1155463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArchonAres</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1154461-gateway-lair-traits?p=1155403#post1155403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Preparing a few areas for lair similarity is ideal, but being able to create similarity of at least some sort on the fly is a good deal. I think that a sufficient amount of broken things scattered over an area could easily simulate razored, but I'd rule that you need to spend your action spreading them before it was enough.<br /> <br /> I'm now imagining a beast who uses a Sunforce spotlight with a disco ball.</div> </div> </div> </div>An action spent creating similarity with a Lair Trait with your gear or powers seems appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T12:56:03-07:00","id":1155492,"title":"","content":"You'd probably need to check with your ST on how extreme it needs to be to qualify as resonant with a lair trait, I mean a broken bottle in a parking lot is probably not going to qualify for jagged.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T13:54:29-07:00","id":1155517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1154461-gateway-lair-traits?p=1155492#post1155492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'd probably need to check with your ST on how extreme it needs to be to qualify as resonant with a lair trait, I mean a broken bottle in a parking lot is probably not going to qualify for jagged.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably not. On the other hand, an handful broken bottles or a broken glass window in a room would in all likelihood qualify for Jagged or Razored, and for the former so would qualify overturned and broken furniture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T04:51:32-07:00","id":1211740,"title":"","content":"Sorry to Necro, but Would dragging someone highup into the air with Wings of the Raptor be enough to Trigger Exposed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T16:58:56-07:00","id":1212059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1154461-gateway-lair-traits?p=1211740#post1211740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry to Necro, but Would dragging someone highup into the air with Wings of the Raptor be enough to Trigger Exposed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably. Especially if there is inclement weather.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T20:14:32-07:00","id":1212120,"title":"","content":"The new Atavisms in BPG gave us a number of options for inflicting Traits, so it seems an appropriate time to revisit the thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T03:36:02-07:00","id":1212195,"title":"","content":"Death of Light could trigger Poor Light and Darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T04:19:41-07:00","id":1212209,"title":"","content":"Plague Bearer can trigger diseased and the minor Version.<br /> Storm-lashed can trigger Electrified, perhaps blizzard, downpour or hurricane.<br /> Titanic blow could certainly trigger jagged, razoured or unstable. <br /> Vengeful earth could potentially trigger crushing or engulfing?<br /> Illusion of Safety could trigger No Exit at Low Satiety.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T10:13:26-07:00","id":1213099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1154461-gateway-lair-traits?p=1212120#post1212120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The new Atavisms in BPG gave us a number of options for inflicting Traits, so it seems an appropriate time to revisit the thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. In addition to and to build up on the ideas provided by Anteros and Wormwood (thanks to both), I'd say:<br /> Caught in the Webs and Crushing Coils can trigger Crushing and Engulfing.<br /> Death of Light is indeed custom-fitted to trigger Poor Light and Darkness.<br /> The Low Satiety version of Illusion of Safety can trigger Sealed Exits.<br /> Plague Bearer is custom-fitted to trigger Diseased (I'm not aware of any minor version of this Trait).<br /> Vengeful Earth can trigger Unstable, its Low Satiety version is explictly told to cause Earthquake, and its Satiety Expenditure version can trigger Crushing and Engulfing.<br /> Weakness Exposed can trigger Exposed (certainly the Satiety Expenditure version, potentially even the normal one).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 04-29-2018, 05:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T13:33:17-07:00","id":1213169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1154461-gateway-lair-traits?p=1213099#post1213099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Low Satiety version of Illusion of Safety can trigger Sealed Exits.<br /> Plague Bearer is custom-fitted to trigger Diseased (I'm not aware of any minor version of this Trait).</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, Sealed Exits, not No Exit was the name.<br /> Infected is the minor version of Diseased imho, introduced as one of the new Lair Traits in the Player's Guide.<br /> Good points, totally lost sight of the Earthquake Lair Trait. Could Titanic Blow on Satiety Expenditure also trigger that?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T15:12:44-07:00","id":1213195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1154461-gateway-lair-traits?p=1213169#post1213169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Infected is the minor version of Diseased imho, introduced as one of the new Lair Traits in the Player's Guide.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'd forgotten the BPG adds a few extra Lair Traits as well, sorry. You are totally spot-on about Infected. As it concerns the other new Traits, You Are Alone seems a natural trigger for Isolated. The right kind of sound effects being recorded and then played out at high volume or imitated with Siren's Treacherous Song may trigger Murmurs. No idea about how to trigger the other Traits, if any.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Good points, totally lost sight of the Earthquake Lair Trait. Could Titanic Blow on Satiety Expenditure also trigger that? </div> </div> </div>IMO, definitely yes. As you said, damage to nearby props may even trigger Jagged or Razored, although it depends on the right kind of stuff being around in the first place.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 04-29-2018, 06:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T16:39:35-07:00","id":1213221,"title":"","content":"For the sake of completeness and reference, I've added the recently discussed ideas and relevant BPG Atavisms to the OP list.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}